# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# In QEMU: the network stack PD with no
# seed ring says it is not ready and never brings its interface up. The PDs
# start in priority order: the timer, the driver, then the stack.
NOWAYOS: timer: starting
NOWAYOS: virtio-net: starting
NOWAYOS: virtio-net: ready on transport 7, MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56
NOWAYOS: net-stack: starting
# AC 3: no seed, no interface.
NOWAYOS: net-stack: not ready: no seed ring (region not mapped: no <map> in the system description sets `nowayos_rw_region_5_vaddr`): no interface brought up

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match),
# including in the second after the last line above: a fault reported by the
# Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic, a PD giving up, the
# interface brought up or a lease taken - smoltcp never runs on its default
# seed - or a queue error.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!interface up
!net-stack: DHCP lease
!net-stack: dropped so far
!queue:
